a map while he was training.

258
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:47,577
After him came Franky
about ten days ago now.

259
00:16:47,660 --> 00:16:50,457
But he headed back out to go see
if your ship was doing all right.

260
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:52,837
I hope that means the
Sunny is in good shape.

261
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:55,397
Of course, there isn't
a single scratch on it.

262
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,127
We finished the coding, too.

263
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:58,597
That's good to hear.

264
00:16:58,680 --> 00:17:01,057
Just make sure you give
credit where credit's due.

265
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:03,937
Even if you don't, there's
no shame in a wound of honor.

266
00:17:04,020 --> 00:17:06,180
It's time for some R &R!

267
00:17:06,940 --> 00:17:09,528
Who knew you'd be so
dedicated to the cause?

268
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:12,822
Your stubbornness came in handy.

269
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:14,099
You mean my looks?

270
00:17:15,660 --> 00:17:17,954
Don't mention it, I owe you one anyway.

271
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:20,117
Come rain or shine, it changed nothing.

272
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:23,177
Dangerous pirates from all
over came to take that ship.

273
00:17:23,260 --> 00:17:26,537
Didn't matter how bad I was hurt,
I defended it day after day.

274
00:17:26,620 --> 00:17:29,257
Cause I knew all these
bruises would be worth it.

275
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:31,200
You're so amazing, sir.

276
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:32,617
Pirates messed you up?

277
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:34,777
Come on, what's the
real story here, Devil?

278
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:35,978
Don't be impatient.

279
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:38,297
I'm trying to build up the
suspense here, you know.

280
00:17:38,380 --> 00:17:40,137
You see, what happened
was the Navy showed up.

281
00:17:40,220 --> 00:17:42,117
The third member of your
crew to arrive was Nami.

282
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:43,030
Nami!

283
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:46,042
That's great, is she still here?

284
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:49,337
She decided to kill time by
getting some shopping done.

285
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:52,538
Come on, don't you want to
hear the rest of my story?

286
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:59,237
The fourth one to arrive was Usopp
three days ago, who also went into town,

287
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:01,877
followed by Chopper,
who showed up yesterday.

288
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:02,977
Brooks made it, too.

289
00:18:03,060 --> 00:18:05,477
He's putting on a concert
for the islanders today.

290
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:06,390
No way.

291
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:10,157
You're the last to stop by,
which makes seven in total.

292
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,777
Not that I expected any less,

293
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:15,137
but almost the entire crew
has made it back in good time.

294
00:18:15,220 --> 00:18:16,050
That's right.

295
00:18:16,133 --> 00:18:18,179
Only Nico, Robin, and Luffy remain.

296
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:20,377
Getting to this island
in the first place is

297
00:18:20,460 --> 00:18:23,048
a difficult task for
any crew to accomplish.

298
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:24,857
And yet, you've made it twice.

299
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:25,770
What can I say?

300
00:18:25,853 --> 00:18:28,311
You must be eager to see each other again.

301
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:29,250
Yeah.

302
00:18:29,333 --> 00:18:32,797
And by the way, I still can't believe
you trained Luffy while we were gone.

303
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:34,860
He must be crazy strong now.

304
00:18:35,820 --> 00:18:38,017
He's been on his own
these last six months.

305
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:40,557
I can't wait to see how
his skills have developed.

306
00:18:40,640 --> 00:18:41,657
Now that you...

307
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:42,920
mention it...

308
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:47,097
I can't wait to see how Nami's
developed, if you know what I'm saying!

309
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:49,140
I should have expected that.

310
00:18:53,740 --> 00:18:54,700
Hey, guys!

311
00:18:55,020 --> 00:18:56,079
What's the matter?

312
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:57,480
Come on, talk to me!

313
00:18:57,720 --> 00:19:01,437
I thought you'd be more excited to
see me, but you're acting weird.

314
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:05,217
From the looks of things, you've all
changed a lot over these last two years.

315
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:08,737
But I mean, we're still friends,
so why are you ignoring me?

316
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:10,760
You, man, it's not leaving.

317
00:19:11,100 --> 00:19:13,777
Oh, you must be shy because
of how much I've changed, too.

318
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:18,257
And if you ask me, that furball knows
a little too much about us Straw Hats,

319
00:19:18,340 --> 00:19:19,417
if you know what I mean.

320
00:19:19,500 --> 00:19:20,330
Yeah, I do.

321
00:19:20,413 --> 00:19:21,937
And you gotta wonder why that is.

322
00:19:22,020 --> 00:19:24,020
Maybe we can find the answer here.

323
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:27,300
No, it can't be!

324
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:34,249
That's the real deal, cotton
candy-loving Tony Tony Chopper!

325
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:35,677
The pet's coming home.

326
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:38,057
So we all look a little
different than we used to.

327
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:38,970
Who cares?

328
00:19:39,280 --> 00:19:41,437
He must have been abandoned
on this island when they

329
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:44,177
died and he's been living
in the wild ever since.

330
00:19:44,260 --> 00:19:46,597
And now he's following
us around because he

331
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:48,997
thinks his masters have
finally come back for him.

332
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:51,786
We should ditch the mutt
and take him instead.

333
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:56,177
If we have their real pet, no one will
ever doubt we're the Straw Heads again.

334
00:19:56,260 --> 00:19:57,090
Sounds good.

335
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:58,070
What's he eat?

336
00:19:58,153 --> 00:19:59,177
Probably cotton candy.

337
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:00,789
We ain't got none of that.

338
00:20:02,420 --> 00:20:03,250
Get it!

339
00:20:03,333 --> 00:20:04,749
We don't need you no more!

340
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:10,320
Come here, boy. You hungry?

341
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,420
Yum, right?

342
00:20:15,220 --> 00:20:16,837
You're kind of freaking me out!

343
00:20:16,920 --> 00:20:17,750
Now!

344
00:20:21,140 --> 00:20:21,970
Robin!

345
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:24,300
Hey! Stop! Come back!

346
00:20:24,540 --> 00:20:26,400
Who were those creeps? Oh, no!

347
00:20:26,620 --> 00:20:28,091
This is a real emergency!

348
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:29,751
What are we gonna do now?

349
00:20:29,940 --> 00:20:32,528
I guess we should tell
Captain Luffy, right?

350
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:34,657
Maybe he knows how to handle this mess.

351
00:20:34,740 --> 00:20:35,570
Wait!

352
00:20:35,653 --> 00:20:37,297
I didn't know Luffy was
back on the island already!

353
00:20:37,380 --> 00:20:41,140
You're right, and we'll have new
recruits by now. That's great!

354
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:43,757
With the extra might,
we'll save Robin for sure!

355
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:45,546
Let's go get our friend back!

356
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,280
Calling from Sabaori!

357
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:50,991
We've secured Nico Robin!

358
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:54,944
We've also caught some fox thing
that won't stop biting her head!

359
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,020
It's been a while.

360
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:59,969
Surely the others have
made it back by now.

361
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:05,530
Hey!

362
00:21:05,613 --> 00:21:06,443
Are you all right?

363
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:08,660
Hey, why did he do that?

364
00:21:08,820 --> 00:21:13,640
He just shot her out of the
blue Come on, we'll get a doctor

365
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:16,100
You what is wrong with you?

366
00:21:16,260 --> 00:21:19,300
She didn't do a damn
thing to deserve that. Uh,

367
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:22,577
I thought you were
someone else I said sorry,

368
00:21:22,660 --> 00:21:28,097
so here's the deal I'm looking for some
punks who crossed me and made a run for it a

369
00:21:28,180 --> 00:21:30,657
red-haired woman and
a guy with a long nose

370
00:21:30,740 --> 00:21:34,200
So you just shot her
That's normal for you?

371
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:35,700
This won't end well.

372
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:37,254
Straw Hat's a monster.

373
00:21:38,180 --> 00:21:39,010
Eh?

374
00:21:39,093 --> 00:21:39,997
You wanna fight about it?

375
00:21:40,080 --> 00:21:41,962
Cause I got plenty more bullets.

376
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:45,160
Your choice, pal.

377
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:50,880
Don't blame me.

378
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:52,041
Blame your nose.

379
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:53,990
Hey!

380
00:21:54,073 --> 00:21:54,977
We'll get some help!

381
00:21:55,060 --> 00:21:55,890
Stay with me!

382
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:59,280
Find those punks now,
or I'll shoot you too!

383
00:22:00,840 --> 00:22:03,460
We got a reputation to uphold here!

384
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:05,960
We gotta show this place who's boss!

385
00:22:26,340 --> 00:22:27,170
Oops.

386
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,697
Didn't see you there.

387
00:22:28,780 --> 00:22:30,680
Sorry about that. See ya.

388
00:22:31,900 --> 00:22:33,320
That guy's insane.

389
00:22:33,640 --> 00:22:36,464
Either that or he doesn't
know who Strawhide is.

390
00:22:36,900 --> 00:22:38,840
He's a dead man either way.

391
00:22:41,180 --> 00:22:42,660
Get back here!

392
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:02,900
There in the distance
is Sabo Odi Archipelago.

393
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:07,028
Forgive me, Luffy, but we will
have to say our goodbyes here.

394
00:23:07,160 --> 00:23:10,748
We cannot let anyone discover
the nature of our relationship.

395
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:16,180
I've prepared a disguise for you.

396
00:23:16,620 --> 00:23:17,580
Are you kidding?

397
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,217
I can't pull that look off.

398
00:23:19,300 --> 00:23:23,640
Perhaps, but I would still feel more
at ease if you took it. All right.

399
00:23:24,700 --> 00:23:25,920
You must be careful.

400
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:28,299
Keep your face hidden at all times.

401
00:23:29,860 --> 00:23:33,137
The world may believe you've
been dead these last two years,

402
00:23:33,220 --> 00:23:37,377
but that won't stop anyone from recognizing
you the first time you get into trouble.

403
00:23:37,460 --> 00:23:41,457
So if you ever want to set sail
again, you'll take my advice to heart.

404
00:23:41,540 --> 00:23:43,720
Thanks. I'll try. You're welcome.

405
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:48,297
Now, for supplies, I've loaded your
backpack with 50 changes of clothes,

406
00:23:48,380 --> 00:23:50,677
1,000 lunches, handkerchiefs, and tissues.

407
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:54,357
You'll also find three years' worth of
water, snacks, and bugbite ointment.

408
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:57,037
There's also five years'
worth of towels, toothbrushes,

409
00:23:57,120 --> 00:23:59,197
plenty of soaps, hand creams,
and lots of silverware.

410
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:00,809
That is entirely too much!

411
00:24:03,920 --> 00:24:06,449
Well, I hope you can
find all your friends.

412
00:24:06,600 --> 00:24:09,953
Thanks again for getting me
here and all the other stuff.

413
00:24:10,100 --> 00:24:11,997
We were more than happy to help you.

414
00:24:12,080 --> 00:24:14,517
Your most difficult trials
may still be ahead of you.

415
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:17,297
I hear that Sabo Odi has
become a den of crime.

416
00:24:17,380 --> 00:24:18,560
And because of that,

417
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:22,517
the Navy has been keeping a tight watch
over the goings-on there as late, my boy.

418
00:24:22,600 --> 00:24:24,365
So be sure to take extra care.

419
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:25,550
Right.

420
00:24:25,633 --> 00:24:26,957
If you ever need assistance,

421
00:24:27,040 --> 00:24:29,337
the full force of the
Kuja pirates will come

422
00:24:29,420 --> 00:24:31,777
rushing to your aid at a moment's notice.

423
00:24:31,860 --> 00:24:33,978
Please don't hesitate to call on us.

424
00:24:36,380 --> 00:24:38,617
Also, would you be
willing to do me a favor?

425
00:24:38,700 --> 00:24:39,540
Yeah, maybe.

426
00:24:39,740 --> 00:24:41,317
As long as it's not getting married.

427
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:42,230
No, no.

428
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:46,800
All I ask is that when you leave,
you do so without saying farewell.

429
00:24:47,900 --> 00:24:48,730
That all?

430
00:24:48,813 --> 00:24:51,297
I've never said that to
anyone before, so sure.

431
00:24:51,380 --> 00:24:53,321
Besides, I want to see you again.

432
00:24:57,720 --> 00:24:59,480
Alright, I'm out of here!

433
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:00,880
Bye, hurry!

434
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:02,100
You take care!

435
00:25:02,400 --> 00:25:03,480
You take care!

436
00:25:04,300 --> 00:25:05,320
Oh, my.

437
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:07,400
He wants to see me again.

438
00:25:07,860 --> 00:25:10,980
That's practically a proposal.

439
00:25:11,740 --> 00:25:12,860
No, it's not.

440
00:25:16,180 --> 00:25:19,417
Hancock told me I got to stay
out of trouble and lay low.

441
00:25:19,500 --> 00:25:21,324
I don't want to fight this guy.

442
00:25:21,880 --> 00:25:22,710
Hey, dummy.

443
00:25:22,793 --> 00:25:24,444
Did you run into me on purpose?

444
00:25:25,100 --> 00:25:25,930
Oh, no.

445
00:25:26,180 --> 00:25:28,121
He's going to kill that poor guy.

446
00:26:02,060 --> 00:26:03,460
PIANO PLAYS

447
00:26:06,740 --> 00:26:07,800
Hi, Sunny.

448
00:26:15,560 --> 00:26:17,089
Sorry to keep you waiting.

449
00:26:17,340 --> 00:26:18,811
I hope you aren't lonely.

450
00:26:20,840 --> 00:26:22,620
You're as lovely as ever.

451
00:26:24,100 --> 00:26:24,930
Huh?

452
00:26:25,340 --> 00:26:26,170
Ow!

453
00:26:29,140 --> 00:26:31,460
Now who is that gorgeous lady?

454
00:26:32,140 --> 00:26:36,380
It's Robin, of course,
our super archaeologist!

455
00:26:41,720 --> 00:26:43,780
Boy, did I miss you!

456
00:27:03,740 --> 00:27:05,920
You haven't changed a bit, Franky.

457
00:27:06,200 --> 00:27:07,437
Is that a joke, sister?

458
00:27:07,520 --> 00:27:08,760
I'm a brand new man!

459
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:10,440
No, I'm more than a man.

460
00:27:10,580 --> 00:27:12,521
I'm the stuff dreams are made of.

461
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:15,740
Gaze upon this fantastic transformation,

462
00:27:16,060 --> 00:27:18,707
the likes of which this
world has never seen!

463
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:20,300
Yeah, baby!

464
00:27:20,720 --> 00:27:22,960
I'm beyond human comprehension!

465
00:27:24,420 --> 00:27:25,260
Fair enough.

466
00:27:25,540 --> 00:27:28,517
Though I might argue that you've been
that way for quite some time now.

467
00:27:28,600 --> 00:27:29,430
Huh?

468
00:27:29,513 --> 00:27:32,120
So I'm not just a freak,
I'm a super freak?

469
00:27:32,380 --> 00:27:34,580
Ha ha, you're gonna make me blush!

470
00:27:42,820 --> 00:27:44,644
This is the coating, I take it?

471
00:27:46,440 --> 00:27:47,480
It's like jelly.

472
00:27:48,520 --> 00:27:52,638
Yep, took a little longer than we
expected, but Rayleigh did his part.

473
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:54,762
Bottom of the sea, here we come!

474
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:56,677
After everyone gets back, of course.

475
00:27:56,760 --> 00:28:00,360
Speaking of which, I saw
Rayleigh at the bar. Oh, yeah?

476
00:28:00,700 --> 00:28:01,917
What number were you?

477
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:03,118
Who are we missing?

478
00:28:03,360 --> 00:28:04,580
I was number eight.

479
00:28:05,060 --> 00:28:07,020
So the only one left is him.

480
00:28:07,720 --> 00:28:08,550
Oofy.

481
00:28:08,633 --> 00:28:11,537
Well, I'm sure our captain
will show up soon enough.

482
00:28:11,620 --> 00:28:13,420
Ship's ready whenever he is.

483
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:18,080
New weapon's ready, too.

484
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:22,040
That sounds just splendid.

485
00:28:22,380 --> 00:28:24,357
By the way, where's everyone else, Issie?

486
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:27,180
Usopp and Sanji stopped by here earlier.

487
00:28:27,660 --> 00:28:30,037
Usopp's picking up some fuel for the trip.

488
00:28:30,120 --> 00:28:32,940
Sanji's getting groceries,
of course. I see.

489
00:28:33,180 --> 00:28:36,062
I ran into something
interesting on the way over.

490
00:28:36,440 --> 00:28:37,800
Have you seen these?

491
00:28:39,480 --> 00:28:41,200
It's for a concert today.

492
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:43,380
He's calling himself Soul King.

493
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:46,040
Yeah, there's a story behind that.

494
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:47,259
He's big news now.

495
00:28:47,460 --> 00:28:49,989
They're selling his
TDs all over the place.

496
00:28:52,820 --> 00:28:55,060
He's left the darkness far behind.

497
00:28:56,280 --> 00:28:59,877
He rose up from those foggy seas
and now he's a shining star.

498
00:28:59,960 --> 00:29:03,842
His fans raise his name to the
heavens if you'll pardon my poetry.

499
00:29:09,740 --> 00:29:12,197
He didn't say anything about this to me.

500
00:29:12,280 --> 00:29:15,617
But he's making a lot of
people happy with his music.

501
00:29:15,700 --> 00:29:18,300
He might not want to be a pirate anymore?

502
00:29:20,420 --> 00:29:24,680
It's no mystery, just rock with me.

503
00:29:26,260 --> 00:29:28,560
And you'll see why I'm the king.

504
00:29:31,360 --> 00:29:35,980
It is in your skeleton, cause
calcium is all that you need.

505
00:29:39,300 --> 00:29:45,460
So dish that fat and protein, make your
body mean and lean. Got milk? Got milk?

506
00:29:46,140 --> 00:29:48,017
Got milk?

507
00:29:48,100 --> 00:29:51,620
My soul is flowing out of my head.

508
00:29:57,860 --> 00:30:00,154
So what are you gonna say for yourself?

509
00:30:00,360 --> 00:30:04,419
You can't tell me you didn't know
who I was when you crashed into me.

510
00:30:04,720 --> 00:30:05,940
Why do it?

511
00:30:06,120 --> 00:30:08,637
Were you just trying to
make a fool out of me?

512
00:30:08,720 --> 00:30:12,040
Cause if so, I don't like
being shown up in public.

513
00:30:12,820 --> 00:30:17,380
After all, I have a reputation and a
400 million buried bounty to uphold.

514
00:30:18,100 --> 00:30:20,840
But you can make it up to me, by kneeling.

515
00:30:21,420 --> 00:30:24,008
Beg for your life and
I might feel generous.

516
00:30:31,560 --> 00:30:32,390
Yo!

517
00:30:32,473 --> 00:30:33,303
Fisherman, you in?

518
00:30:33,386 --> 00:30:37,200
Looking for some good stock at a
low price. Huh? It's the place?

519
00:30:40,100 --> 00:30:41,512
Hey, you run this shack.

520
00:30:43,640 --> 00:30:44,699
What's the matter?

521
00:30:44,960 --> 00:30:46,195
It's something awful.

522
00:30:46,980 --> 00:30:48,800
That green-haired man's gone.

523
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:50,080
Aw, crap.

524
00:30:50,520 --> 00:30:51,957
All right, old man, spill it.

525
00:30:52,040 --> 00:30:54,317
I can't believe this has happened to me.

526
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:57,077
Well, you see, uh...

527
00:30:57,160 --> 00:30:58,460
Hey, Gramps.

528
00:30:58,660 --> 00:31:00,237
I was looking to do some fishing.

529
00:31:00,320 --> 00:31:01,150
Huh?

530
00:31:01,233 --> 00:31:05,413
No offense, young man, but I wouldn't
exactly beg you as the fishing type.

531
00:31:06,120 --> 00:31:07,557
Normally, you'd be right.

532
00:31:07,640 --> 00:31:09,857
I'm supposed to be meeting
some friends on this island,

533
00:31:09,940 --> 00:31:11,257
but they haven't made it yet.

534
00:31:11,340 --> 00:31:13,046
So I'm bored out of my skull.

535
00:31:13,340 --> 00:31:16,634
So I need something to keep
me entertained while I wait.

536
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:19,580
You think you can help
me out or not? Sure.

537
00:31:19,820 --> 00:31:21,557
I'll finish getting
everything we need ready

538
00:31:21,640 --> 00:31:24,346
and then meet you on my
boat right over there.

539
00:31:25,180 --> 00:31:27,280
And that's all I said to him.

540
00:31:27,520 --> 00:31:32,180
To be clear, did this guy have three
swords and a belly warmer? Yes, he did.

541
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:34,537
And he had a deep scar on his eye, too.

542
00:31:34,620 --> 00:31:35,502
How'd you know?

543
00:31:37,180 --> 00:31:38,010
Scars knew.

544
00:31:38,093 --> 00:31:38,923
Is this him?

545
00:31:39,440 --> 00:31:40,270
Yeah.

546
00:31:40,353 --> 00:31:42,277
He said he'd been waiting
on some friends to show.

547
00:31:42,360 --> 00:31:43,400
That must be you.

548
00:31:43,560 --> 00:31:45,340
Well, I wouldn't go that far.

549
00:31:45,980 --> 00:31:48,477
You see, I told him to
wait on my fishing boat?

550
00:31:48,560 --> 00:31:51,117
While I was getting ready, and
I pointed right at the thing.

551
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:54,700
But when I came outside,
he'd made a huge mistake. No!

552
00:31:55,340 --> 00:31:56,170
Young man!

553
00:31:56,840 --> 00:31:58,016
You've got it wrong!

554
00:31:58,160 --> 00:32:00,900
You're on a pirate ship! No, men.

555
00:32:01,020 --> 00:32:03,957
It's time we set sail for the
new world we've been dreaming of.

556
00:32:04,040 --> 00:32:05,040
The wait is over!

557
00:32:05,600 --> 00:32:06,780
Come on, please!

558
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:08,136
You have to wake up!

559
00:32:08,320 --> 00:32:10,085
You've got on the pirate ship!

560
00:32:11,340 --> 00:32:16,500
Since they went underwater, I guess
they were headed to Fishman Island.

561
00:32:21,080 --> 00:32:22,080
That idiot.

562
00:32:28,140 --> 00:32:31,937
Should have known him showing up
here first was too good to be true.

563
00:32:32,020 --> 00:32:34,757
Wouldn't be Zoro if he
didn't get lost somewhere.

564
00:32:34,840 --> 00:32:36,077
Aren't you worried at all?

565
00:32:36,160 --> 00:32:37,777
They might kill him on that ship.

566
00:32:37,860 --> 00:32:38,690
It's fine.

567
00:32:38,773 --> 00:32:39,637
Don't get worked up.

568
00:32:39,720 --> 00:32:42,014
This is pretty standard fare, actually.

569
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:45,437
Better than usual, even, since we
know where he's going for once.

570
00:32:45,520 --> 00:32:47,457
Now, would you mind selling
me some fish already?

571
00:32:47,540 --> 00:32:49,246
I don't think you understand.

572
00:32:49,740 --> 00:32:50,900
Whoa! See that?

573
00:32:51,660 --> 00:32:52,490
Huh?

574
00:32:52,700 --> 00:32:53,920
Look at the waves!

575
00:32:54,120 --> 00:32:55,414
Something's coming up!

576
00:32:57,660 --> 00:32:58,537
But what?!

577
00:32:58,620 --> 00:33:00,280
It must be huge!

578
00:33:12,520 --> 00:33:13,980
That's a galleon ship!

579
00:33:14,320 --> 00:33:17,677
He must have had poor coating and
was crushed under the water pressure.

580
00:33:17,760 --> 00:33:19,497
No, it has to be the work of Sea Kings.

581
00:33:19,580 --> 00:33:22,877
But it looks like it's been cut
in half, like someone attacked it.

582
00:33:22,960 --> 00:33:23,790
No way.

583
00:33:24,060 --> 00:33:25,377
Just think for a second.

584
00:33:25,460 --> 00:33:26,697
Who in the world could do that?

585
00:33:26,780 --> 00:33:27,610
Damn you.

586
00:33:27,693 --> 00:33:28,523
Tell me why.

587
00:33:28,606 --> 00:33:32,676
How could you just ruin our dreams
of reaching the new world like this?

588
00:33:33,880 --> 00:33:35,360
Call it a twist of fate.

589
00:33:35,620 --> 00:33:37,617
That's what brought this
plague upon your ship.

590
00:33:37,700 --> 00:33:40,700
And there's no one for you
to blame but yourselves.

591
00:33:40,960 --> 00:33:42,660
Are you kidding me?

592
00:33:43,940 --> 00:33:45,600
Who the heck is that guy?

593
00:33:45,720 --> 00:33:47,300
A great back already.

594
00:33:47,760 --> 00:33:49,760
And he's still a pain in the ass.

595
00:34:00,500 --> 00:34:02,540
That wasn't my ride.
